{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01520",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 5.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.28,
      "end_seconds": 11.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.13,
      "end_seconds": 18.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Yeah, it's chest tightness when I walk uphill. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.71,
      "end_seconds": 26.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.9,
      "end_seconds": 37.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "Probably one week. Yeah. I did try to ignore it for a while. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.96,
      "end_seconds": 44.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.77,
      "end_seconds": 49.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.34,
      "end_seconds": 53.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Any pain in your jaw as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.2,
      "end_seconds": 72.42,
      "duration_seconds": 18.22,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, four weeks. As for pain in my jaw, mild, I'd say. Exertion definitely sets it off. It settles a little with resting. Breathlessness on exertion was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.66,
      "end_seconds": 80.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "Have you had chest tightness when you walk uphill before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.38,
      "end_seconds": 86.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last year. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.51,
      "end_seconds": 94.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Have you had any fainting, palpitations, leg swelling or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.29,
      "end_seconds": 102.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "I mean, I haven't had fainting, palpitations, leg swelling or pain at rest, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.19,
      "end_seconds": 106.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.94,
      "end_seconds": 109.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.11,
      "end_seconds": 114.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.43,
      "end_seconds": 119.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.16,
      "end_seconds": 120.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.67,
      "end_seconds": 126.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "I take rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.66,
      "end_seconds": 134.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.83,
      "end_seconds": 138.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Yes, walnuts, it gives me hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.65,
      "end_seconds": 148.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.86,
      "end_seconds": 160.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.86,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I hardly move around during the day. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.26,
      "end_seconds": 172.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.91,
      "end_seconds": 177.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.41,
      "end_seconds": 199.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.02,
      "end_seconds": 214.18,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for nearly five years now. I have high cholesterol. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.84,
      "end_seconds": 218.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.69,
      "end_seconds": 234.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.09,
      "end_seconds": 257.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 121 over 71, pulse 86, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.21,
      "end_seconds": 262.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.09,
      "end_seconds": 266.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.29,
      "end_seconds": 289.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Your heart sounds are normal and the pulses are all present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.94,
      "end_seconds": 294.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.71,
      "end_seconds": 320.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I'd lean towards stable angina. I think an ECG makes sense here, for chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.44,
      "end_seconds": 323.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.71,
      "end_seconds": 359.82,
      "duration_seconds": 35.11,
      "text": "For this, glyceryl trinitrate spray, 400 micrograms, when needed, long term. It's for chest tightness. Stop and rest when the tightness starts, and use the spray if it does not ease in a few minutes. I think the chest pain clinic should see you too. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'd like you back after the tests. Alright, anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.24,
      "end_seconds": 364.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}